msgid ""
"Build a learning experiment for the latest version of Qiskit noise learning"
msgstr ""

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Build a learning experiment"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Build a learning experiment {#build-a-learning-experiment}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This tutorial demonstrates how to build a standard learning experiment from "
"scratch, and use it to learn a model from simulated noisy data.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1.  '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Define a gate set on a ring of qubits\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '2.  '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Choose a 2-local Pauli-Lindblad model\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '3.  '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Build the learning experiment\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '4.  '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Generate circuits\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '5.  '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Set up local simulation\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '6.  '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Run the program\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '7.  '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Analyze the data\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Running on real hardware\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  The circuits below are simulated locally, so this walkthrough needs no IBM Quantum® credentials. To alternatively run it on a real device:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '  *   '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Step 1**: replace "
"[`FakeMarrakesh`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/fake-"
"provider-fake-marrakesh \"(in Qiskit Runtime IBM Client)\") with a real "
"backend.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  *   **Step 5**: pass that backend as the executor’s mode, and drop the simulator options.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"define-a-gate-set-on-a-ring-of-qubits\" />\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"1. Define a gate set on a ring of qubits {#1-define-a-gate-set-on-a-ring-of-"
"qubits}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Build a [`QiskitGateSet`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-noise-"
"learning/generated/gate-sets-qiskit-gate-"
"set#qiskit_noise_learning.gate_sets.QiskitGateSet "
"\"qiskit_noise_learning.gate_sets.QiskitGateSet\") from a backend "
"[`Target`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.Target)"
" and a subset of its qubits — here a twelve-qubit ring of "
"[`FakeMarrakesh`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/fake-"
"provider-fake-marrakesh \"(in Qiskit Runtime IBM Client)\") — then add one "
"gate to it: a layer of six `CZ` gates covering that ring. By default the "
"gate set is initialized with a preparation gate `P` and a measurement gate "
"`M`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<DoqAdmonition type=\"note\" title=\"Running on real hardware\">\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "</DoqAdmonition>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Call [`draw()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-noise-"
"learning/generated/gate-sets-gate-"
"set#qiskit_noise_learning.gate_sets.GateSet.draw "
"\"qiskit_noise_learning.gate_sets.GateSet.draw\") to see the gate on the "
"device topology: the ring of qubits in the gate set, and which pairs of them"
" the gate entangles.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"choose-a-2-local-pauli-lindblad-model\" />\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"2. Choose a 2-local Pauli-Lindblad model {#2-choose-a-2-local-pauli-"
"lindblad-model}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Decide which Pauli-Lindblad generators the noise is allowed to have with a "
"[`PauliLindbladModel`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-noise-"
"learning/generated/models-pauli-lindblad-"
"model#qiskit_noise_learning.models.PauliLindbladModel "
"\"qiskit_noise_learning.models.PauliLindbladModel\"). Build that generator "
"set from the gate set’s connectivity with "
"[`k_local()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-noise-"
"learning/generated/models-pauli-lindblad-"
"model#qiskit_noise_learning.models.PauliLindbladModel.k_local "
"\"qiskit_noise_learning.models.PauliLindbladModel.k_local\") — here every "
"2-local Pauli on connected qubit pairs of the unitary gate, and single-qubit"
" Paulis for preparation and measurement.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Display the unknown parameter count for the noise model of each gate.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"build-the-learning-experiment\" />\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "3. Build the learning experiment {#3-build-the-learning-experiment}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Assemble an [`Experiment`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-noise-"
"learning/generated/experiment-builder-"
"experiment#qiskit_noise_learning.experiment_builder.Experiment "
"\"qiskit_noise_learning.experiment_builder.Experiment\") by composing "
"builder stages. Each stage reads what earlier stages wrote, so order "
"matters:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Observe design matrix rank:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"generate-circuits\" />\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "4. Generate circuits {#4-generate-circuits}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Compile the experiment with an "
"[`ExecutorCircuitGenerator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-noise-"
"learning/generated/circuit-generator-executor-circuit-"
"generator#qiskit_noise_learning.circuit_generator.ExecutorCircuitGenerator "
"\"qiskit_noise_learning.circuit_generator.ExecutorCircuitGenerator\"), "
"generating a [`QuantumProgram`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-"
"runtime/quantum-program-quantum-program \"(in Qiskit Runtime IBM Client)\") "
"— one parameterized template circuit per fragment depth.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Draw a template circuit to inspect.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![../\\_images/4088c7e98baeb5b56925c6c1f276159582c5f7040fbba76de438b919210bcc5f.png](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-"
"noise-"
"learning/4088c7e98baeb5b56925c6c1f276159582c5f7040fbba76de438b919210bcc5f.avif)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"set-up-local-simulation\" />\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "5. Set up local simulation {#5-set-up-local-simulation}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To define the noise model for simulation, we use the generators already in "
"the model with random rates to construct a "
"[`PauliLindbladMap`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.PauliLindbladMap).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Those maps are as wide as the device, since the model is expressed in "
"`backend`’s qubit indexing, but the simulator wants each map to be as wide "
"as the gate it applies to, with Pauli indices running over the gate’s qubits"
" in ascending physical order. Narrow them with "
"[`keep_qubits()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.PauliLindbladMap#keep_qubits),"
" which traces out everything off the ring:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The simulator names a layer’s noise by the box instruction the layer was "
"built from, which "
"[`to_instruction()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-noise-"
"learning/generated/gate-sets-qiskit-"
"gate#qiskit_noise_learning.gate_sets.QiskitGate.to_instruction "
"\"qiskit_noise_learning.gate_sets.QiskitGate.to_instruction\") returns for "
"any gate in the gate set. Pair each box with its map, use the stabilizer "
"simulation method, and set `seed_simulator` to make the simulated data "
"reproducible:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"run-the-program\" />\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "6. Run the program {#6-run-the-program}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Run the program, then format the results with "
"[`collect()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-noise-"
"learning/generated/circuit-generator-executor-circuit-"
"generator#qiskit_noise_learning.circuit_generator.ExecutorCircuitGenerator.collect"
" "
"\"qiskit_noise_learning.circuit_generator.ExecutorCircuitGenerator.collect\"),"
" to produce a [`Fit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-noise-"
"learning/generated/analysis-fit#qiskit_noise_learning.analysis.Fit "
"\"qiskit_noise_learning.analysis.Fit\") — the container the analysis stages "
"read from and write to.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This step is the same whether the executor is pointed at a simulator or at a"
" real device.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"analyze-the-data\" />\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "7. Analyze the data {#7-analyze-the-data}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Build an analysis pipeline around nonnegative least squares fitting of the "
"model.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Plot the measured observable means against their fitted exponentials, one "
"subplot per `CZ` pair, to see whether the decays being fitted are "
"exponential at all.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Swap `exponential_fit` for `model_prediction` to compare the same data "
"against the decays implied by the rates that came out of the non-negative "
"least squares solve.\n"
msgstr ""
